{
  "number": 2882,
  "title": "Graph forwards reasoning blocks into downstream node input",
  "url": "https://github.com/strands-agents/harness-sdk/issues/2882",
  "state": "closed",
  "created_at": "2026-06-20T22:44:10Z",
  "closed_at": "2026-06-25T19:30:26Z",
  "body": "## Summary\n\n`Graph` pass reasoning content from an upstream node into a downstream node input. I wanted to check whether this is expected, because it breaks on Bedrock and also seems surprising from a graph-composition perspective.\n\nIn my case, one node uses a reasoning-capable model, then a second node depends on its output. The second node receives the first node full content, including `reasoningBlock` content, as part of its input. Bedrock then rejects the request because reasoning content is present on a user message.\n\n## What I am seeing\n\nWith a simple two-node graph:\n\n1. Node A uses a reasoning-capable Bedrock model.\n2. Node B depends on Node A.\n3. Node A returns content that includes a reasoning block.\n4. Graph dependency resolution forwards that content into Node B.\n5. Node B request fails because the downstream user message contains reasoning content.\n\nThe Bedrock error is:\n\n```text\nUser messages cannot contain reasoning content\n```\n\nLooking at SDK `1.6.0`, this seems to happen because graph dependency input resolution forwards dependency content directly:\n\n```ts\ndeps.push(new TextBlock(`[node: ${edge.source.id}]`), ...ns.content);\n```\n\n## Minimal repro shape\n\n```ts\nconst graph = new Graph({\n  nodes: [\n    { id: \"reasoner\", executor: reasoningAgent },\n    { id: \"curator\", executor: normalAgent },\n  ],\n  edges: [{ source: \"reasoner\", target: \"curator\" }],\n});\n\nawait graph.run(\"Introduce yourself and explain your strengths.\");\n```\n\nWhere `reasoningAgent` uses a reasoning-capable Bedrock model, such as DeepSeek R1 or a Claude thinking model.\n\n## Question\n\nIs this forwarding behavior intentional?\n\nIf it is, is there a recommended way to configure graph handoff so downstream nodes receive only the upstream node final/output content?\n\nIf it is not intentional, would filtering `reasoningBlock` content during graph dependency input resolution be the right fix?\n",
  "labels": [
    "bug",
    "python",
    "area-multiagent",
    "area-model"
  ],
